  {
    "name": "support-policy",
    "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/envoyproxy/envoy/v1.40.2/RELEASES.md",
    "fetched_at": "2026-11-11T08:35:22.632Z",
    "status": 200,
    "sha256": "95af65ff86c5e40405abd4d5abc33930e3e126289f19fa3cf37193c0cc5364b5",
    "excerpts": [
      {
        "line": 1,
        "text": "# Release Process"
      },
      {
        "line": 5,
        "text": "Active development is happening on the `main` branch, and a new version is released from it."
      },
      {
        "line": 7,
        "text": "## Stable releases"
      },
      {
        "line": 9,
        "text": "Stable releases of Envoy include:"
      },
      {
        "line": 11,
        "text": "* Major releases in which a new version a created directly from the `main` branch."
      },
      {
        "line": 12,
        "text": "* Minor releases for versions covered by the extended maintenance window (any version released in the last 12 months)."
      },
      {
        "line": 17,
        "text": "  * Bugfixes, deemed worthwhile by the maintainers of stable releases."
      },
      {
        "line": 19,
        "text": "Major releases happen quartely and follow the schedule below. Security fixes typically happen"
      },
      {
        "line": 20,
        "text": "quarterly as well, but this depends on the number and severity of security bugs. Other releases"
      },
      {
        "line": 23,
        "text": "### Security releases"
      },
      {
        "line": 27,
        "text": "of stable releases backport them to the remaining supported stable releases."
      },
      {
        "line": 31,
        "text": "All other security and reliability fixes can be nominated for backporting to stable releases"
      },
      {
        "line": 38,
        "text": "Envoy release maintainers will try to review and include any pending proposed backports prior to"
      },
      {
        "line": 39,
        "text": "patch releases. Backports can also be proposed directly, by raising a PR against the relevant"
      },
      {
        "line": 40,
        "text": "release branch, eg `release/v1.37`."
      },
      {
        "line": 42,
        "text": "When raising a backport, please raise against **all** supported branches, that are affected."
      },
      {
        "line": 45,
        "text": "commits while tracking the upstream release branch, before landing."
      },
      {
        "line": 50,
        "text": "Release branches are published as part of the security schedule described below, and immediately"
      },
      {
        "line": 51,
        "text": "prior to a `main` release."
      },
      {
        "line": 53,
        "text": "### Release management"
      },
      {
        "line": 55,
        "text": "Major releases are handled by the maintainer on-call and do not involve any backports."
      },
      {
        "line": 56,
        "text": "The details are outlined in the \"Cutting a major release\" section below."
      },
      {
        "line": 57,
        "text": "Security releases are handled by a Release Manager and a Fix Lead. The Release Manager is"
      },
      {
        "line": 61,
        "text": "team and is responsible for coordinating the overall release. This includes identifying"
      },
      {
        "line": 62,
        "text": "issues to be fixed in the release, communications with the Envoy community, and the"
      },
      {
        "line": 63,
        "text": "actual mechanics of the release itself."
      },
      {
        "line": 65,
        "text": "| Quarter |       Release Manager                                          |         Fix Lead                                                         |"
      },
      {
        "line": 90,
        "text": "## Major release schedule"
      },
      {
        "line": 92,
        "text": "In order to accommodate downstream projects, new Envoy releases are produced on a fixed release"
      },
      {
        "line": 96,
        "text": "| Version |  Expected  |   Actual   | Difference | End of Life |"
      },
      {
        "line": 128,
        "text": "### Cutting a major release"
      },
      {
        "line": 130,
        "text": "* Take a look at open issues tagged with the current release, by"
      },
      {
        "line": 135,
        "text": "  particularly risky PRs until after the release is tagged. This is because we aim for main to be"
      },
      {
        "line": 136,
        "text": "  at release candidate quality at all times."
      },
      {
        "line": 137,
        "text": "* Do a final check of the release note fragments in [changelogs/current](changelogs/current):"
      },
      {
        "line": 139,
        "text": "  * Check to see if any security/stable version release notes are duplicated in"
      },
      {
        "line": 140,
        "text": "    the major version release notes. These should not be duplicated."
      },
      {
        "line": 141,
        "text": "  * Switch the repo to \"release\" mode by running `bazel run @envoy_repo//:release`. This tool"
      },
      {
        "line": 142,
        "text": "    will create a commit with the necessary changes for a release."
      },
      {
        "line": 143,
        "text": "  * Update the [RELEASES](RELEASES.md) doc with the relevant dates. Now, or after you cut the"
      },
      {
        "line": 144,
        "text": "    release, please also make sure there's a stable maintainer signed up for next quarter,"
      },
      {
        "line": 145,
        "text": "    and the deadline for the next release is documented in the release schedule."
      },
      {
        "line": 148,
        "text": "* Once the tests have passed, and the PR has landed, CI will automatically create the tagged release and corresponding release branch."
      },
      {
